# Panels whose .apply hook changes the system rather than the session, and
# so has to run as root. The session runs as tsuser and the image carries no
# sudo; tp-apply hands these to tp-root-apply.service, which runs nothing
# that is not named here (it reads this list itself, as root).
#
# Keyboard, mouse, display, sound, background and the rest are absent on
# purpose: they talk to the X server and must run inside the session.
bluetooth
datetime
firewall
language
network
power
printers
restartplan
security
snmp
sshd
usb
